* `(-1, 0, -9, -8)` is irreducible: `F(u, v) = −N((u + 0v) − vz)` in `ℤ[z]`, `z³ = (-9) z + (-8)`. Its only solution `(−1, 0)` comes from `RankOneSources.K43.source0` (unit generation and the Skolem zero set).
* `(0, -3, 0, -43)` is reducible, solved by `ReducibleThue` (factor, Bezout pair, integer square root).

The class-list premise is proved by `ClassListProof.classList_of` (parameters by `norm_num`,
transports by the kernel), and `PositiveKCurve.complete_of_sols` reads off the points.
-/

